  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/af1f5efcb6090c7ace2347d7f3a4076c87adc9f2</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev/commit/af1f5efcb6090c7ace2347d7f3a4076c87adc9f2"/>
    <title>
        feat(zai): serve GLM-5.3-Flash on zai and zai-coding-plan (#5535)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-08-26T18:47:18Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40026523?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>Nick-CHI</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/Nick-CHI</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;feat(zai): serve GLM-5.3-Flash on zai and zai-coding-plan (#5535)

The lab entry models/zhipuai/glm-5.3-flash.toml already exists, but no
provider hosts it, so GLM-5.3-Flash does not appear in the catalog.

Both Z.ai endpoints serve it today (verified 2026-08-26 against GET
/models and a chat completion on each):

- zai (https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4) — per-token pricing, matching the
  published $0.075 / $0.25 per M with $0.015 cached input
- zai-coding-plan (https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4) — included in
  the GLM Coding plans and billed against plan credits, so cost 0,
  consistent with the sibling glm-5.3 / glm-5.3-highspeed entries

Reasoning is on by default; reasoning_effort low|high|max is honored and
{&amp;quot;thinking&amp;quot;: {&amp;quot;type&amp;quot;: &amp;quot;disabled&amp;quot;}} suppresses it, so the effort options
mirror the base GLM-5.3 family.

bun validate passes.

Co-authored-by: Nick-CHI &amp;lt;puasinternet225@gmail.com&amp;gt;
Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) &amp;lt;noreply@anthropic.com&amp;gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
